# Line endings are LF, everywhere, on every platform.
#
# This repository was mixed for a long time -- 309 files CRLF, 180 LF, and one
# that was both -- which made every editor that "helpfully" normalised a file
# produce a diff of the whole thing. `eol=lf` settles it in the index and in
# the working tree, so a checkout on Windows gets LF too and nothing has an
# opinion to express.
#
# `text=auto` still detects a binary by content and leaves it alone, so nothing
# added later needs a rule of its own unless git guesses wrong about it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# What `embed` carries is bytes, and a checkout that turned a CRLF in one into an
# LF would change the program built from it. `text=auto` guesses from content
# and would guess right about most of these, which is not the same as always.
*.bin binary
